msgstr ""

#: build/admin/tax.js:8
msgid "Tax shipping like the items it carries"
msgstr ""

#: build/admin/tax.js:8
msgid "Shipping’s price is shared out by what the items cost, and each share is taxed at those items’ rates, as EU VAT asks: shipping books and lamps together is taxed partly at the books’ rate. Untaxed items’ share is not taxed. Otherwise shipping is taxed at the tax group of its way to ship."
msgstr ""

#: build/admin/tax.js:8
msgid "Ask businesses for their VAT or tax number"
msgstr ""

#: build/admin/tax.js:8
msgid "The number goes on the order and the invoice. Businesses in another EU country than yours, with a VAT number the EU’s VIES service confirms, buy without VAT and account for it themselves (reverse charge); when VIES cannot be asked, VAT is charged. Numbers from the UK, Switzerland, Norway, Australia, New Zealand and Canada are checked by their check digit, and one that fails is left out."
msgstr ""

#: build/admin/tax.js:8
msgid "States that tax at the seller’s address"
msgstr ""

#: build/admin/tax.js:8
msgid "Use a country and a state code, such as US-TX."
msgstr ""

